  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN241.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What [SHE] said to the confidante [who comforted] HER who had undergone changes during the separation.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN241.1">
        <l>tuṉiyiṉ ṟiyainta tuva<supplied>rā</supplied> naṭpi</l>
        <l>ṉi<supplied>ṉi</supplied>ya ramma <supplied>vi</supplied>vareṉa muṉiyātu</l>
        <l>nalkuvar nalla <supplied>kūṟi ya</supplied>lkalum </l>
        <l>piriyāk kātalō ṭuḻaiya rākiya</l>
        <l>namarmaṉ vāḻi tōḻi yuyarmicai</l>
        <l>mūṅki liḷamuḷai tiraṅkak kāmpiṉ</l>
        <l>kaḻainaral viya<supplied>la</supplied>kam vempa maḻaimaṟan</l>
        <l>taruvi yāṉṟa veruvaru naṉantalaip</l>
        <l>pēe veṇṭēr peyalcet tōṭit</l>
        <l>tā<supplied>a</supplied>m paṭṭa taṉimutir peruṅkalai</l>
        <l><supplied>pu</supplied>lampeyarn tuṟaital cellā talaṅkutalai</l>
        <l>viruntiṉ veṅkāṭṭu varunti vaiku</l>
        <l>matta nellit tīñcuvait tiraḷkā<supplied>y</supplied></l>
        <l>vaṭṭak ka<supplied>ḻa</supplied>ṅkiṟ ṟā<supplied>a</supplied>yt tuyttalaic</l>
        <l>cemmuka ma<supplied>n</supplied>ti yāṭu</l>
        <l><supplied>nīṇ</supplied>mara maruṅkiṉ malaiyiṟan tōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="3a">He who grants [his presence]</l>
        <l corresp="2">without aversion, so that [we] say : “sweet, ah, is he,</l>
        <l corresp="1">in undivided intimacy that is enjoyable without disgust”,</l>
        <l rend="indent5" corresp="3b-d">talking good [words] all night,</l>
        <l corresp="4">who was the one close to [us] with inseparable love,</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c">he is ours indeed, oh friend,</l>
        <l corresp="16d">– he who,</l>
        <l corresp="8">in the frightening vast area where the waterfalls ceased,</l>
        <l corresp="7">the rains having forgotten [them], so that the wide interior is hot, rattling with stems</l>
        <l corresp="5d-6">in shafts while the young sprouts dry on the bamboo on the high hillocks,</l>
        <l corresp="13a">on the road,</l>
        <l corresp="10">where the solitary aging big male monkey that suffers from thirst,</l>
        <l corresp="9">runs after the fearful mirage, thinking it rain,</l>
        <l corresp="12">[and] is kept in suffering in the hot wilderness, like a guest</l>
        <l corresp="11">[its] head swaying, unable to keep changing the region,</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="16">traversed the mountains on the side of tall trees,</l>
        <l corresp="14d-15">where the soft-headed red-faced female monkey plays,</l>
        <l>spreading the sweet-tasting round unripe gooseberry fruits</l>
        <l corresp="13b-14c">like round Molucca beans (cast as an omen).</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

